[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Webhook authentication and outage recovery
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Webhook requests always require a valid, current `Paygate-Signature`; replay-token
[?2004l[?2004h> headers do not bypass verification. During secret rotation, any configured signing
[?2004l[?2004h> secret may match any supplied `v1` signature. Verified retries are deduplicated by
[?2004l[?2004h> `event_id`, including ignored events, without rewriting stored payloads or auditing again.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> For trusted outage payloads already stored in `ops/backlog/`, use:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h>     npm run replay-backlog
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> This local recovery tool skips processed event IDs and obeys the refund-storm guard
[?2004l[?2004h> in `config/refunds.json`: at most 20 events per run, at least 120 seconds between runs.
[?2004l[?2004h> Repeat after the required interval until it reports zero remaining events; do not
[?2004l[?2004h> relax the guard to drain a backlog. Internal HTTP replay still requires a bearer key
[?2004l[?2004h> with `refunds:replay` permission.
